  The row for THE_LIABILITY_TABLE.md, in its format:
     | 0.82 | 0.0019 | pressure | UNGC Local Volume groups, 26 groups, 333 members |

  [PASS] C1 the group rung BREAKS the reading in which the deficit is a low-acceleration phenomenon.  These groups sit at 10^-4 to 10^-2 a_0 -- below every X-ray group and cluster row but one -- and carry a SMALLER boost than nearly all of them.  So the residual is not a function of acceleration; it appears where the baryon budget is MODELLED, not where it is COUNTED   (14 of 14 X-ray group/cluster rows sit ABOVE this rung's boost of 0.82, and they do so at HIGHER accelerations (median 0.111 a_0 against this rung's 0.0019 a_0))

